1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:03,860
一只僵尸，翻不过这堵八米高的墙
One zombie can't climb an eight-metre wall.

2
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:07,907
可几千只僵尸，会把彼此当成梯子
But a few thousand will use each other as a ladder.

3
00:00:09,167 --> 00:00:11,130
《僵尸世界大战》里
In World War Z,

4
00:00:11,130 --> 00:00:14,541
尸潮就是这样叠成人山，翻进城里的
that's how the horde piles into a mountain and spills over.

5
00:00:14,541 --> 00:00:17,506
每一只都在找路、推挤、攀爬
Every one of them is pathing, shoving and climbing.

6
00:00:17,506 --> 00:00:20,285
游戏要怎么同时算这么多个？
How does a game compute that many at once?

7
00:00:21,585 --> 00:00:25,197
这一期，我们从《守望先锋》的 ECS 讲起
This episode starts with the ECS behind Overwatch.

8
00:00:27,497 --> 00:00:31,244
最直觉的写法，是给每只僵尸一个对象
The intuitive way is one object per zombie:

9
00:00:31,244 --> 00:00:36,115
位置、速度、血量、动画，再写一个 update
position, velocity, health, animation, plus an update method.

10
00:00:36,675 --> 00:00:38,880
可这些对象散落在内存各处
But those objects are scattered across memory.

11
00:00:38,880 --> 00:00:41,672
CPU 每次整块读进 64 字节
The CPU always fetches 64 bytes at a time,

12
00:00:41,672 --> 00:00:43,142
大部分都用不上
and most of them go unused.

13
00:00:43,702 --> 00:00:45,866
我在这台电脑上测了一下
I measured it on this machine:

14
00:00:45,866 --> 00:00:49,422
一百万个对象，光是挪一步就要 37 毫秒
just moving a million objects one step takes 37 milliseconds,

15
00:00:49,422 --> 00:00:51,277
超过了一整帧的时间
more than a whole frame.

16
00:00:52,577 --> 00:00:54,640
《守望先锋》用的是另一种架构
Overwatch uses a different architecture.

17
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:59,010
这是首席玩法程序员 Tim Ford 在 GDC 2017 的演讲
Here is lead gameplay programmer Tim Ford at GDC 2017:

18
00:00:59,310 --> 00:01:03,460
实体其实只是一个 ID，对应一组组件
An entity is really just an ID that corresponds to a collection of components.

19
00:01:03,460 --> 00:01:06,910
组件存储游戏状态，没有行为
Components store game state and have no behaviors.

20
00:01:06,910 --> 00:01:09,710
系统拥有行为，不存储游戏状态
Systems have behaviors and store no game state.

21
00:01:10,260 --> 00:01:12,991
组件里没有函数，系统里没有字段
Components have no functions; systems have no fields.

22
00:01:13,551 --> 00:01:15,973
每个系统只关心几种组件
Each system only cares about a few components:

23
00:01:15,973 --> 00:01:20,297
挂机检测只处理同时拥有连接、输入和统计的实体
the AFK check runs on entities that have a connection, input and stats;

24
00:01:20,297 --> 00:01:24,102
AI 机器人没有连接组件，自然就被跳过
an AI bot has no connection, so it's simply skipped.

25
00:01:24,662 --> 00:01:29,463
《守望先锋》客户端大约有 46 个系统、103 种组件
The Overwatch client has about 46 systems and 103 component types.

26
00:01:29,463 --> 00:01:32,664
对他们来说，最大的好处是控制复杂度
For them, the big win was keeping complexity under control.

27
00:01:33,964 --> 00:01:37,689
实体多到上万时，ECS 还有另一个好处
Once there are tens of thousands of entities, ECS has another payoff:

28
00:01:37,689 --> 00:01:41,075
同一种组件，可以紧挨着存成一列数组
each component type can sit packed in a single array.

29
00:01:41,735 --> 00:01:43,736
系统从头到尾扫一遍
A system sweeps it from start to end,

30
00:01:43,736 --> 00:01:46,070
读进来的每个字节都有用
and every byte it fetches gets used.

31
00:01:46,070 --> 00:01:50,405
同样一百万个，只要 3.8 毫秒，快了将近十倍
The same million entities take 3.8 milliseconds, almost ten times faster.

32
00:01:51,905 --> 00:01:53,645
可光跑得快还不够
Speed alone isn't enough:

33
00:01:53,645 --> 00:01:57,442
一万只僵尸要是各自算一遍寻路，还是算不过来
ten thousand zombies each running their own pathfinding is still too much.

34
00:01:58,002 --> 00:01:59,291
办法是流场
The answer is a flow field:

35
00:01:59,291 --> 00:02:02,354
从目标出发，把整条街的距离算一遍
compute the distance to the goal across the whole street once,

36
00:02:02,354 --> 00:02:05,094
每个格子存一个指向目标的箭头
and every cell stores an arrow pointing the way.

37
00:02:05,754 --> 00:02:08,605
每只僵尸只读脚下的那一个箭头
Each zombie reads only the arrow under its feet.

38
00:02:08,605 --> 00:02:11,455
地图只算一次，僵尸再多也不怕
The map is solved once, no matter how many zombies there are.

39
00:02:12,955 --> 00:02:14,824
人山是怎么叠起来的？
So how does the mountain form?

40
00:02:14,824 --> 00:02:18,096
每一步，先数一数每个格子里有几只僵尸
Every step, count the zombies in each cell,

41
00:02:18,096 --> 00:02:20,744
和上一期鱼群用的是同一张网格
the same grid trick the flocks used.

42
00:02:21,304 --> 00:02:24,121
格子越挤，僵尸就站得越高
The more crowded the cell, the higher a zombie stands;

43
00:02:24,121 --> 00:02:27,126
被墙挡住的，会爬到同伴身上
those blocked by the wall climb onto the others,

44
00:02:27,126 --> 00:02:29,943
坡越堆越高，最后漫过墙头
and the slope rises until it spills over the top.

45
00:02:30,603 --> 00:02:33,097
据 Game Informer 报道
According to Game Informer,

46
00:02:33,097 --> 00:02:36,304
《僵尸世界大战》为尸潮专门写了 Swarm 引擎
World War Z's Swarm Engine was built for the hordes,

47
00:02:36,304 --> 00:02:37,610
同屏最多约五百只
handling up to about five hundred zombies on screen.

48
00:02:38,070 --> 00:02:40,240
它内部怎么实现并没有公开
Its internals aren't public;

49
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:42,409
这里演示的是一种常见思路
what you see here is one common approach.

50
00:02:44,109 --> 00:02:49,248
整个尸潮就是七个系统，每帧按顺序跑一遍
The whole horde is seven systems, run in order every frame:

51
00:02:49,248 --> 00:02:54,620
生成、计数、流场、攀爬、移动、回收、动画
spawn, count, flow, climb, move, recycle, animate.

52
00:02:55,280 --> 00:02:57,197
八千一百九十二只僵尸
Eight thousand one hundred ninety-two zombies,

53
00:02:57,197 --> 00:02:59,703
每一只都只是几列数组里的一行
each just one row across a few arrays.

54
00:03:01,603 --> 00:03:04,426
每只僵尸，都要转身朝向目标
Every zombie turns to face its goal.

55
00:03:04,426 --> 00:03:08,132
可如果要转向的，是一百万块太阳能板呢？
But what if what needs turning is a million solar panels?

56
00:03:09,032 --> 00:03:11,326
下一期：《戴森球计划》
Next time: Dyson Sphere Program,

57
00:03:11,326 --> 00:03:14,275
让无数块太阳能板一起追着太阳转
and countless solar panels tracking the sun together.

58
00:03:14,535 --> 00:03:17,382
而这一切，还得从一只僵尸说起
And all of it starts, once again, with a single zombie.
